lines+=['## 2. Generalized family description','','Compute a×b by determinant, minors and signed products. Form sqrt(sum of all three squared components). Equate this to the supplied positive magnitude; square, collect/factor, solve for every real x. A radio response is the complete root set; ordered blanks are individual scalar fragments. Squaring is safe because the supplied magnitude is positive; substitute every root into the complete original magnitude equation.','','## 3. Component map and complete banks','','Each source above maps every field and every observed option. Source profiles are complete opaque observed expression patterns, with root rescaling as a reproducible recipe. This transformation does not establish original distractor intent. They are available only when explicitly requesting their source-layout template, never mixed into the authored default bank. Correct answers are independently derived from all components before any bank is rendered. Whole-bank collisions or invalid roots are failures, not replaced options.','','The authored complete radio bank is: full ±r; +r only; −r only; ±r² (omit final square root); ±sqrt(r) (take another square root). It is selected before sampling, contains exactly five options, and is rejected as a whole if its complete sets collide. Hard defaults use the observed single/two-blank layouts, so no distractors are fabricated for blanks.','','## 4. Reusable Markdown/value templates','','The public API source templates accept scale in {1/2,1,2}. Every polynomial monomial involving the unknown is multiplied by scale^degree, including determinant entries, minor entries, evaluated signed products, expanded norm squares, solving equations, and all answer values. Complete equation sets and vector coordinates are independently read back and verified. Basis i,j,k, TeX commands, prose and field keys are protected. Scaling is mathematical substitution rather than a branch returning source JSON. Narrative root claims and requested scalar fragments divide by scale. Original ordered intermediate operations remain present, including any source-specific redundant-row omission. The last source aligned solving row can remain scale·x=root, with the new x isolated in the final narrative. At scale=1 the full source string is naturally reproduced except documented repairs.','','Authored easy bounds: a=(p,1,cx), b=(0,1,dx), p∈{1,2,3}, c∈{1,2,3}, d∈{1,2}, c≠d, positive root r∈{2,3,4}. The two nonzero homogeneous cross components and nonzero constant component cannot disappear. Authored moderate bounds: a=(cx,p,q), b=(dx,u,v), c∈{2,−2,3}, d∈{1,−1}, p∈{2,3}, q∈{1,2,3}, u∈{1,2}, v∈{−2,−1,1,2}; r∈{2,3,4,sqrt2,sqrt3,sqrt5}. Exactly two variable cross components are required. Authored hard bounds: a=(cx,p,q), b=(r,0,u), c,p,r,u∈{1,2,3}, q∈{1,2,3,4,5}, root offset from quadratic center ∈{0,1,2}; reject zero linear coefficient, root magnitude >10, root denominator >4 or primitive quadratic coefficient magnitude >100. All defaults and explicit calls enforce the same guards. Coordinates contain no floats. Source substitution extensions retain coordinate magnitude ≤12 and denominator ≤4 and the same solving structure; these observed-recipe extensions are explicitly separate from authored bounds.','','Numeric products in authored determinant expansion always use visible \\cdot with grouped second factors. Changed observed recipes scale complete monomials, never concatenate numeric factors. No source numeric juxtaposition is introduced.','','### Source anomalies and repair accounting','','q-19783 has no correct key, no solution, no difficulty, and prints a dot product. Dot magnitude is |10+3x²|=sqrt705, which does not have any displayed source root set. The corrected cross equation has cross=(−7x,11x,−5), squared magnitude 170x²+25=705, hence x=±2. The raw prompt and missing fields remain in source.json and review.md. The supported observed-q-ID profile performs the minimum cross-operator repair, retains the calculator note and all five original values, and supplies a documented authored moderate solution/key. Original designation match is unavailable, not reported as passed.','','q-103540 evaluates determinant signs incorrectly in its final displayed vector. Correct cross=(−5,4x,−x); replacing the second and third signs and the corresponding squared-substitution row leaves magnitude and all answers unchanged. The raw solution remains preserved. Supported output has 19/20 raw-exact complete source solutions and 20/20 supported sequence reproductions after this repair; public :raw replay has 20/20 exact present solutions. No source solution exists for the remaining one.','','Decoded source bytes contain zero actual doubled backslashes across all 75 answer strings. The earlier report confused JSON serialization escapes with decoded string content; that claim is withdrawn. Normal output only changes two Unicode ± occurrences to TeX \\pm (both in q-19783), giving 73/75 raw-byte exact answer values and 20/21 raw-byte complete banks in supported output. All 75 raw values and all 21 raw complete banks are preserved exactly by the public observed-q-ID:raw profiles. This Unicode presentation normalization is independent of the two mathematical source repairs. Raw replay has 21/21 exact full prompts and 21/21 exact full solutions-or-absence; it preserves q-19783 missing rating, key and solution, and q-103540 erroneous vector/norm rows. Raw profiles are explicitly evidence-only and ineligible for learner generation; they do not claim anomalous mathematics is valid. All raw profiles also accept changed scale parameters via the same monomial and answer-set rescaling recipes.','','No plots: template plot rating none. Steps 5/7 need no renderer.']
